                "new_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities for small examples.\n\n## numbers.total\n\n`total(values)` returns the sum of all non-`None` values in the iterable.\n\n- `None` values are ignored.\n- Zero and negative numbers are included.\n- If the input is empty, or contains only `None`, the result is `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## labels.normalize\n\n`normalize(value)` cleans up simple labels.\n\n- Leading and trailing whitespace is removed.\n- Internal spaces are preserved.\n- All letters are converted to lowercase.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")   # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")      # \"\"\nnormalize(\"X  Y\")    # \"x  y\"\n```\n"
