  "final_files": {
    "numbers.py": "def total(values):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of non-None values.\n\n    None values are ignored. Zero and negative numbers are kept.\n    An empty input (or one containing only None) returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(v for v in values if v is not None)\n",
    "labels.py": "def normalize(value):\n    \"\"\"Normalize a string by trimming outer whitespace and lowercasing.\n\n    Leading and trailing whitespace is removed, internal spaces are kept.\n    \"\"\"\n    return value.strip().lower()\n",
    "README.md": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities for small examples.\n\n## numbers.total\n\n`total(values)` returns the sum of all non-`None` values in the iterable.\n\n- `None` values are ignored.\n- Zero and negative numbers are included.\n- If the input is empty, or contains only `None`, the result is `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## labels.normalize\n\n`normalize(value)` cleans up simple labels.\n\n- Leading and trailing whitespace is removed.\n- Internal spaces are preserved.\n- All letters are converted to lowercase.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")   # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")      # \"\"\nnormalize(\"X  Y\")    # \"x  y\"\n```\n",
    "test_numbers.py": "import unittest\nfrom numbers import total\n\nclass NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_total(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([2, None, -1, 0]), 1)\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([None]), 0)\n",
    "test_labels.py": "import unittest\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nclass LabelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_normalize(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize(' A B '), 'a b')\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize('  '), '')\n"
